From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the pointer goes where a page says it does

A desktop whose focus follows the cursor has to take the cursor with it
when a key moves the focus. sway calls it `mouse_warping` and does it
itself; here the shell is a page, and a page can read where the pointer
is and cannot put it anywhere -- so the focus a press moved was handed
straight back by the first pointer event over the window it came from.

`warpPointer` is the message that answers it, and this is the one place
it needs a file Chromium owns. The rest is the fork's own: the mojom,
the Blink method, `ControlChannel::WarpPointer`, and the two halves in
`//components/domicile:pointer_warp` and
`//chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_pointer_warp.cc`.

THE SINK IS BOUND HERE FOR THE KEYMAP'S REASON NEXT DOOR. A cursor is
moved through the aura WindowTreeHost the page's view belongs to, which
is the UI thread's, and the channel is read on the IO thread. Binding it
here -- where the UI thread is already the current one, and where the
frame is -- is what keeps //content and //chrome out of
//components/domicile:control_channel, which deliberately has neither.

By id rather than by frame, because the callback runs on the other side
of a thread hop: a RenderFrameHost may not be carried across threads,
and a page that closed in the meantime is a lookup that answers nothing.

WRITTEN BY HAND, AGAINST THE SERIES RATHER THAN IN A CHECKOUT, so its
post-image blob is not known and is left zeroed: there was no Chromium
tree to read it from. Regenerate the series with `scripts/extract.sh`
once this has been applied on a tree -- `scripts/test-patch-series-chain.sh`
is what will say so, on the next patch that touches this file.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
index b00851ab8b..0e90e7074e 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.cc
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders.h"
 
 #include "base/task/bind_post_task.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_pointer_warp.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_shell_windows.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/control_channel.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/keyboard_layout.h"
@@ -509,6 +510,16 @@ void PopulateChromeFrameBinders(
                 base::BindPostTask(
                     content::GetUIThreadTaskRunner({}),
                     base::BindRepeating(&domicile::SetProcessKeymap)),
+                // AND WHERE THIS PAGE'S POINTER GOES WHEN IT ASKS. Bound
+                // here for the keymap's reason above: the cursor belongs to
+                // the UI thread, along with the window it is moved within,
+                // and this is where the UI thread already is. The frame goes
+                // in as its id rather than as itself, because what runs on
+                // the far side of that hop may not hold a RenderFrameHost.
+                base::BindPostTask(
+                    content::GetUIThreadTaskRunner({}),
+                    base::BindRepeating(&domicile::WarpPointerIn,
+                                        frame->GetGlobalId())),
                 // AND WHICH WINDOW THIS PAGE IS. A desk of several monitors is
                 // several windows, each loading the same shell, and the only
                 // thing that differs between them is the display they cover.
